# Task I: the SMP samples $F4-$F7 in the middle of its read cycle (bsnes
# SMP::read: a half wait before and after the access, "bus hold delays on CPU
# I/O reads"), not at its end. A CPU port write in the second half of an SPC
# cycle is therefore seen one cycle later. Round the write's SPC timestamp to
# the nearest cycle instead of down, so it lands on the cycle whose read can
# see it. TLK's streaming upload (SPC $19CF / $19E4: CMP A,$F6 / BEQ) races the
# CPU's STX $2142 against that read on every byte pair; with floor rounding
# the SPC won the race ~45% of the time against ~8% in BizHawk.
@@ apu-port-write-half-cycle
<<<<
    uint64_t guest_cycle = rtl_apu_guest_cycle();
    while (!apu_schedulePortWrite(g_snes->apu, port, val, guest_cycle))
